# CAP-4 Module B — Loan Provisioning & Termination
# HTTP client file (IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client)
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. App running: ./mvnw spring-boot:run
#   2. Get a token: run POST /api/v1/auth/dev-token below, copy the token
#      into the @token variable.
#
# Seeded items you can borrow (all entitled for inst_7f3 / usr_dev123):
#   item_env  — SUBSCRIPTION  (open-ended, canPersist=true)
#   item_42   — ELITE         (copy-limited, canPersist=false)
#   item_ab6  — OPEN_ACCESS   (free, canPersist=true)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ─── Step 0: Get a token (dev only — no SAML/OIDC needed) ──────────────────

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/dev-token

# Response 200:
# {
#   "token": "eyJ...",
#   "issuedAt": "2026-08-25T05:35:18Z",
#   "expiresAt": "2026-08-25T06:35:18Z"
# }

### ─── Paste your token here ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJhdWQiOiJ0Zi1hcHAiLCJpbnN0aXR1dGlvbklkIjoiaW5zdF83ZjMiLCJ0b2tlbl91c2UiOiJhY2Nlc3MiLCJjb2xsZWN0aW9ucyI6WyJjb2xfbGF3MjAyNCJdLCJyb2xlcyI6WyJNRU1CRVIiXSwiaXNzIjoidGYtcmVhZGVyIiwiZXhwIjoxNzg3NjM3MDU4LCJ0eXBlIjoiSU5TVElUVVRJT04iLCJpYXQiOjE3ODc2MzYxNTgsInVzZXJJZCI6InVzcl9kZXYxMjMifQ.FMYyWCY7wwVWt369PHcHSRVfvkplIhPW_jA9R5gWoQQ

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### ENDPOINT 1 — POST /api/v1/loans  (borrow)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1a. Borrow a SUBSCRIPTION title → 201 Created
# Returns a new loan. dueAt is null (open-ended). canPersist=true = reader can download.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item_env"
}

# Response 201:
# {
#   "loanId": "loan_ce49cbc6",
#   "itemId": "item_env",
#   "licenceModel": "SUBSCRIPTION",
#   "status": "ACTIVE",
#   "canPersist": true,
#   "borrowedAt": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.196217Z",
#   "dueAt": null,
#   "serverTime": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.196217Z"
# }

###

### 1b. Borrow an ELITE title → 201 Created
# Copy-limited. canPersist=false = read-only (no download). dueAt is set.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item_42"
}

# Response 201:
# {
#   "loanId": "loan_2d1d357f",
#   "itemId": "item_42",
#   "licenceModel": "ELITE",
#   "status": "ACTIVE",
#   "canPersist": false,
#   "borrowedAt": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.196Z",
#   "dueAt": "2026-09-08T05:35:58.196Z",
#   "serverTime": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.196Z"
# }

###

### 1c. Borrow an OPEN_ACCESS title → 201 Created

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item_ab6"
}

###

### 1d. Re-borrow the same title → 200 OK (idempotent)
# Same loanId returned. No second copy claimed. Safe to call on double-tap.

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item_env"
}

# Response 200 — same loanId as 1a:
# {
#   "loanId": "loan_ce49cbc6",
#   ...
# }

###

### 1e. Borrow without a token → 401 UNAUTHENTICATED

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item_env"
}

# Response 401:
# { "code": "UNAUTHENTICATED", ... }

###

### 1f. Borrow an unknown item → 403 NOT_FOUND (no entitlement)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "item_does_not_exist"
}

# Response 403: { "code": "NOT_FOUND", ... }

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### ENDPOINT 2 — GET /api/v1/loans  (personal library listing)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 2a. List all loans (all statuses, newest first)

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Response 200:
# {
#   "loans": [
#     { "loanId": "loan_ce49cbc6", "itemId": "item_env", "licenceModel": "SUBSCRIPTION",
#       "status": "ACTIVE", "canPersist": true, "borrowedAt": "...", "dueAt": null,
#       "returnedAt": null, "expiredAt": null },
#     ...
#   ],
#   "page": 0,
#   "size": 20,
#   "total": 3,
#   "serverTime": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.318963Z"
# }

###

### 2b. Filter by status=ACTIVE

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans?status=ACTIVE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2c. Filter by status=RETURNED

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans?status=RETURNED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2d. Filter by status=EXPIRED

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans?status=EXPIRED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2e. Paginate — page 0, size 2

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans?page=0&size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 2f. Invalid status → 400 VALIDATION_FAILED

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans?status=BOGUS
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Response 400:
# { "code": "VALIDATION_FAILED", "message": "status must be one of ACTIVE, EXPIRED, RETURNED" }

###

### 2g. No token → 401

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### ENDPOINT 3 — POST /api/v1/loans/{loanId}/return
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### Replace loan_ce49cbc6 with a real loanId from step 1a / 2a above.

### 3a. Return an active loan → 200 OK
# Write order: mark RETURNED → release copy → promote next waiter (D-022).

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans/loan_ce49cbc6/return
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Response 200:
# {
#   "loanId": "loan_ce49cbc6",
#   "itemId": "item_env",
#   "status": "RETURNED",
#   "returnedAt": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.355459Z",
#   "serverTime": "2026-08-25T05:35:58.355459Z"
# }

###

### 3b. Return the same loan again → 409 LOAN_NOT_ACTIVE (double-tap is safe)

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans/loan_ce49cbc6/return
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Response 409:
# { "code": "LOAN_NOT_ACTIVE", "message": "This loan is already closed." }

###

### 3c. Return an unknown loanId → 404 NOT_FOUND

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans/loan_does_not_exist/return
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# Response 404: { "code": "NOT_FOUND", ... }

###

### 3d. Return someone else's loan → 403 FORBIDDEN_SCOPE

# (Borrow with a different dev-token user, try to return with this one)
# Response 403: { "code": "FORBIDDEN_SCOPE", "message": "This loan is not yours." }

###

### 3e. No token → 401

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/loans/loan_ce49cbc6/return

###
